# Story 7: Stacked Panes (45s)
# Hook: Stack panes like cards -- flip through them instantly.
# Duration: 45s
# Source: story-07-stacked-panes.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 8

[00:00.0 --> 00:03.0]
Stack panes like cards -- flip through them instantly.

[00:03.0 --> 00:06.0]
Start rysh with a single pane.

[00:06.0 --> 00:10.0]
This is pane 1 -- the bottom of our stack.

[00:10.0 --> 00:16.0]
Ctrl+P, then s creates a stacked pane. It slides on top of the current pane.

[00:16.0 --> 00:22.0]
Do it again -- Ctrl+P, s. Now we have three panes stacked in the same space.

[00:22.0 --> 00:32.0]
Ctrl+S enters stack mode. Press j to go to the next pane in the stack, k to go back.

[00:32.0 --> 00:38.0]
Press Escape to exit stack mode. Your panes stay stacked and ready.

[00:38.0 --> 00:45.0]
Stacked panes give you maximum screen real estate. One column, multiple contexts -- flip through them with j and k.

